title: goblin_cantina_chieftain
---
Fretjaw: No real fights in the cantina. Break a chair, buy two. Fretjaw hates paperwork.
-> What goes on here?
    <<jump goblin_cantina_chieftain__1>>
-> Why a training pit?
    <<jump goblin_cantina_chieftain__2>>
-> Been any trouble with the gate patrols?
    <<jump goblin_cantina_chieftain__gate>>
-> Walk away.
===

title: goblin_cantina_chieftain__1
---
Fretjaw: Jump the tables if you want. Duck by the bar. Bleed on floor, buy a round. And leave those three under the dais alone; they paid already.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump goblin_cantina_chieftain>>
-> Walk away.
===

title: goblin_cantina_chieftain__2
---
Fretjaw: Walls cost money. Pit was already here. Also the floor gets beer on it. You learn fast on beer.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump goblin_cantina_chieftain>>
-> Walk away.
===

title: military_general
---
General: AT EASE, RECRUIT. You are in the Iron Bastion. Parade deck below, offices above. Keep your hands off the medals.
-> What is this place?
    <<jump military_general__1>>
-> Why so many medals?
    <<jump military_general__2>>
-> Ask about the gate annex.
    <<jump military_general__gate>>
-> Who's requesting gate access?
    <<jump military_general__petitions>>
-> Salute and withdraw.
===

title: military_general__gate
---
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "gate.clearance.military")>>
    General: Your clearance stands. SENTINEL is the annex, and the annex dials what the public ring may not. The log reads every dial. So do I.
<<elseif boss_cleared("castle_godwin.wolfenstein")>>
    General: You put down the dog of Castle Godwin. That is a military result, and a military result earns military clearance. The checkpoint downstairs will open for you, and the annex ring answers SENTINEL from any public ring.
    <<command "world.set_flag" "gate.clearance.military" true>>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "gate.known.SENTINEL" true>>
<<else>>
    General: The annex off the parade deck holds our ring. Priority band, logged use, clearance only. Earn a military result and we will talk about clearance.
    General: And keep out of the maintenance crawlway. It is for maintenance, and for nobody who crouches.
<<endif>>
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump military_general>>
-> Salute and withdraw.
===

title: military_general__1
---
General: Iron Bastion, Faction of Steel. We drill downstairs. The upper floors are offices. Avoid the upper floors unless somebody outranks you enough to make it unavoidable.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump military_general>>
-> Salute and withdraw.
===

title: military_general__2
---
General: Three for punctuality. Two for meetings about punctuality. This large one? I authorized it personally.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump military_general>>
-> Salute and withdraw.
===

title: pulse_voyager_captain
---
Captain Pulse: Tie off there, drifter. The stones drift about half a beat every cycle. Miss the timing and you come up under the next one.
-> Where do these stones lead?
    <<jump pulse_voyager_captain__1>>
-> Why park up in the sky?
    <<jump pulse_voyager_captain__2>>
-> Do you carry freight between dimensions?
    <<jump pulse_voyager_captain__freight>>
-> Cast off.
===

title: pulse_voyager_captain__1
---
Captain Pulse: Step on the bright one, then the cracked one. Skip either and the third stone is gone before you reach it.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump pulse_voyager_captain>>
-> Cast off.
===

title: pulse_voyager_captain__2
---
Captain Pulse: We moor up here because the lower current tears anchors loose. Up here the ship only drifts a few feet an hour.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump pulse_voyager_captain>>
-> Cast off.
===

title: tech_bros_disruptor
---
Chadwick III: Welcome to the basement! We're not failing — we're SUBTERRANEAN. Premium iteration depth. We've vertically integrated gravity into the runway. Very capital-efficient.
-> What is this place pivoting toward?
    <<jump tech_bros_disruptor__1>>
-> Why does the boardroom face up?
    <<jump tech_bros_disruptor__2>>
-> Touch grass.
===

title: tech_bros_disruptor__1
---
Chadwick III: Disruption-as-a-service, friend. We disrupt anything that holds still long enough. Our roadmap is a slope. Our slope is the roadmap. Both are pivots. That's a flywheel.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump tech_bros_disruptor>>
-> Touch grass.
===

title: tech_bros_disruptor__2
---
Chadwick III: The boardroom faces up because vision is a direction. Looking down is for accountants. We do not look down. We are the down. It's category-defining.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump tech_bros_disruptor>>
-> Touch grass.
===

title: military_general__petitions
---
General: The castle submits another request for our passenger records every month. One page this time, six pages last time.
General: Haven't signed it. The office that wants it can send somebody up here and explain themselves.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump military_general>>
-> Salute and withdraw.
===

title: goblin_cantina_chieftain__gate
---
Fretjaw: Some checkpoint officer asked for names of all goblins who came through the ring. Fretjaw told him to buy drinks first.
Fretjaw: He left without paying. Got no names, either.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump goblin_cantina_chieftain>>
-> Walk away.
===

title: pulse_voyager_captain__freight
---
Captain Pulse: Small loads, when the weather lets us. The orbital station pays better, but the gate won't take this whole hull.
Captain Pulse: Last trip I sent the crates ahead. Customs held them until I turned up to sign.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump pulse_voyager_captain>>
-> Cast off.
===
